# Build-context hygiene (mirrors the repository root .dockerignore).
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` bakes the developer's node_modules AND the local
# `.env` into the image. A baked `.env` is not just a secret leak: it adds
# INTERNAL_SERVICE_TOKEN (the legacy shared cluster credential) to the container
# environment, which would re-enable the shared-credential fallback and silently
# bypass the per-service INTERNAL_SERVICE_TOKENS map that docker-compose injects
# at runtime. Configuration must come from the orchestrator, never from the image.
node_modules
npm-debug.log*
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.git
.gitignore
README.md
*.md
coverage
.nyc_output
dist
build
